WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.650
Unlike other genres, action movies don't need
to be filled with nuanced performances or

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:06.800
a watertight plot.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.589
If anything, those things just get in the
way of the face-punching.

00:00:10.589 --> 00:00:15.589
All a good action movie needs is a sky-high
bullet budget, some flippy kicks, and kerosene

00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:18.240
burning through its veins from start to finish.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.949
Fortunately, Netflix is jammed full of underrated
action movies.

00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:26.189
If you'd rather see bruised chins than Oscar
wins, this action movie roundup will be right

00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:27.449
up your alley.

00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:28.869
Skin Trade

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:34.351
Dolph Lundgren, Ron Perlman, Michael Jai White,
and Tony Jaa sounds like a dream action movie

00:00:34.351 --> 00:00:38.780
cast if we've ever seen one, and Skin Trade
delivers on that promise in spades.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:43.230
Granted, the plot is pretty flimsy—it's
basically cops and robbers in Thailand—but

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:46.960
the thrill of seeing these action legends
all in one place doesn't wear off.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:52.370
Lundgren manages to keep up with the much
younger and more agile Jaa in some wild action

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:56.629
scenes, and Jai White is, as always, a magnetic
on-screen talent.

00:00:56.629 --> 00:00:58.019
Come for the talent lineup.

00:00:58.019 --> 00:01:00.910
Stay for the insanity and fist fights.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:02.739
Savage Dog

00:01:02.739 --> 00:01:07.190
Scott Adkins is pretty much the undisputed
king of direct-to-DVD action movies these

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:10.970
days, and Savage Dog is an impressive entry
in his filmography.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:15.380
We rarely get to see Adkins in a period piece,
and even though he still mostly just beats

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:18.840
people up, he gets to do it in different costumes
this time.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.620
But beyond the unusual setting, Savage Dog
is still something special.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:26.960
The movie opens with Adkins' character digging
his way out of a shallow grave, which is the

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.200
only way to start a movie like this.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:33.299
The film then goes back in time, catching
us up to the moment of his burial and then

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:38.140
sending him on a brutal path of revenge featuring
some stunning fight sequences.

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:42.659
Adkins' filmography is littered with cool
action hits, but Savage Dog is a clear high

00:01:42.659 --> 00:01:44.000
point.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.439
Bullet to the Head

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:51.080
Released in 2013, Bullet to the Head comes
from Walter Hill, director of the 1979 cult

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.689
classic The Warriors.

00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:57.180
It's pure grindhouse fun, which is exactly
what a Walter Hill action flick starring Sylvester

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.700
Stallone should be.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:03.560
Bullets fly, bodies drop, and cars are blown
to bits over the course of the movie.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:08.190
It's a great time, solidified by Jason Momoa's
role as the film's villain.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.170
You don't want to miss it.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.300
Boyka: Undisputed

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:17.650
Scott Adkins headlines the later installments
of the Undisputed series as Yuri Boyka, a

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.670
prison inmate who participates in a brutal
underground prison fighting ring.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:26.100
Boyka: Undisputed sees Boyka released from
prison and fighting professionally, but the

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:30.520
fight scenes are just as stylish and brutal
as any that came before this in the series.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.190
Four movies in, Undisputed is as fun as it's
ever been.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:36.110
Bring on the next one.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.630
Small Soldiers

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:42.290
Children of the '90s are likely to remember
the toys that spawned from director Joe Dante's

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:46.650
Small Soldiers, along with the crushing disappointment
that they didn't actually come to life and

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.520
try to blow up your house.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.240
"Let me see that weapon.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.040
Standard issue is insufficient."

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:58.921
The film itself is something of a forgotten
gem—and one that's definitely made for a

00:02:58.921 --> 00:03:03.000
younger audience—but an action movie is
an action movie, and this one is actually

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.060
a lot of fun.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:09.090
Small Soldiers is weird, campy, and features
action figures going to war with each other,

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:13.920
which, for most kids, was the best toy-based
combat outside of Toy Commander for the Sega

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.310
Dreamcast.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:17.340
Sky Captain and the World of Tomorrow

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:21.870
In a just world, Sky Captain and the World
of Tomorrow would have been a box office smash

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:25.640
and ushered in a new era of elegant, stylistic
action cinema.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:29.980
Drawing heavily from pulp cinema and comic
books, Sky Captain is a wild romp through

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.130
a steampunk reimagining of a pre-World War
II world.

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:38.260
The titular Sky Captain is a charismatic ace
pilot who leads the daredevil Flying Legion.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:43.380
Played by Jude Law, he's joined by reporter
Polly Perkins and a brief appearance by Angelina

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:47.400
Jolie as the eyepatched Royal Navy officer
Franky Cook.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.950
It's a great cast heading up a fun, visually
inventive action film that deserves a far

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:55.260
larger fan following than it has today.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:56.390
Officer Downe

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:59.230
Want to watch the craziest movie on Netflix?

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:00.400
Officer Downe has you covered.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.980
Adapted from the comic by writer Joe Casey
and artist Chris Burnham, there shouldn't

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:08.420
be a way to translate this insanity from page
to screen.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:11.010
And yet the film manages to pull it off.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:15.180
Starring Kim Coates of Sons of Anarchy fame,
it's a hyperkinetic neon thrill ride that

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.660
plays out like Judge Dredd in a fever dream.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:22.720
This movie has everything: nuns with guns,
an immortal super cop, and a hidden government

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:23.720
conspiracy.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:25.990
What more could you ask for?

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:27.540
Fighting

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:31.770
It's kind of hard to remember the days when
Channing Tatum wasn't a megastar, but back

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:36.400
before Magic Mike and 21 Jump Street, Tatum
appeared in this little-seen gem.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:42.000
Tatum plays the tough-as-nails Shawn, a hustler
who discovers he's a prodigy as a street fighter.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.790
The fight scenes are brutal, no-holds-barred
affairs that translate the intensity of street

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:49.160
fighting to the screen very well.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:53.680
Fighting was never going to win any Oscars,
but it's a very interesting, and often overlooked

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.680
entry in a talented actor's career.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:58.140
Death Sentence

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:02.930
Modern horror master James Wan — of Saw,
Insidious and The Conjuring fame — took

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:08.750
a brief hiatus from the genre in 2007 with
Death Sentence, a Kevin Bacon vehicle that

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:12.780
follows the tried-and-true narrative of a
regular man out for revenge.

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:17.470
When his son is stabbed in a gang initiation
ritual, Bacon's Nick Hume decides to take

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:21.740
the law into his own hands, waging a one-man
war on crime in his city.

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:25.570
It's nothing action fans haven't seen before
— but you haven't seen this kind of film

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:30.740
directed by a wiz like James Wan or with an
actor so effortlessly good as Kevin Bacon.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:36.270
Bacon channels Nick's relentless drive, grief,
and rage in stunning, understated fashion.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:39.930
Throw in John Goodman as the film's villain
and you've got yourself a good time.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:44.450
It may be familiar action movie territory,
but sometimes that just means it's worth the

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:45.450
journey.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.640
Thanks for watching!

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:49.420
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:51.820
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

